<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech Teplarny Brno 9mo net profit dips.</title>
<headline>Czech Teplarny Brno 9mo net profit dips.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for nine-month period</p>
<p>ending September 30, 1996: (in millions of crowns)</p>
<p> Gross profit	     236.887    vs    237.515</p>
<p> Net profit		 169.952    vs    174.738</p>
<p> Operational profit     238.399    vs    236.280</p>
<p>Sales of products</p>
<p>  and services	  1,101.675    vs    977.059</p>
<p> Write-offs		  44.871    vs     40.970</p>
<p> Assets		   1,530.761    vs  1,185.570</p>
<p> Basic capital	    885.650    vs    885.650</p>
<p>Note. Full company name is Teplarny Brno a.s., a heating utility in the Czech Republic's second largest city, Brno.</p>
<p>Britain's Eastern Group is its main shareholder, according to the Czech securities registry, with a 53 percent stake in the firm. Industrial conglomerate Hanson recently bought Eastern Electricity, renamed it Eastern Group and aims to spin it off as part of a separate business under its demerger plans.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
